  "title": "Turkish Parliament Passes Landmark Law to End Conflict with Kurdish Militants",
  "summary": "Turkey’s parliament passed a landmark law to end conflict with Kurdish militants, including a conditional pardon for thousands of fighters who have been captured or detained. This marks a significant step towards peace and reconciliation in the region.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The law includes a conditional pardon for thousands of fighters in the Kurdistan Workers’ Party (KPK) who have been captured or detained.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The law was passed by the Turkish parliament with the aim of ending ongoing violence and promoting peace.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The law includes provisions that could allow for temporary release of captured fighters under specific conditions.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
